# What the core says of spelling, in English. See locales/README.md.

# $name is the name of the dictionary's files: nb_NO. $message says why.
spelling-unreadable = The dictionary { $name } could not be read: { $message }
spelling-encoding = The dictionary { $name } is written in an encoding that cannot be read.
# Stands after "not found:". $language is the language of a map: nb, en-GB.
spelling-dictionary-for = a dictionary for “{ $language }”
spelling-not-a-word = “{ $word }” cannot be added to your words.
spelling-not-a-language = Words of your own cannot be kept for “{ $language }”.
# $language is the language of the list (en, nb); $message says why.
spelling-own-unreadable = Your own words for “{ $language }” could not be read: { $message }
# $path is where the file was moved to, beside where it was.
spelling-own-set-aside = Your own words for “{ $language }” could not be read ({ $message }), so the word was not changed. The file is set aside as { $path }; a word added now begins a new list.
